# clang-tidy configuration for wm2-born-again (D-03, TEST-06).
#
# clang-tidy has NO baseline mechanism -- its only suppression is a per-line
# NOLINT comment, and the errors-list key below promotes whole families at once
# (08-RESEARCH.md Pitfall 8). So D-03 is implemented with two different
# mechanisms: cppcheck gets a checked-in content-hashed baseline, and
# clang-tidy gets this explicit allowlist.
#
# The gate is scripts/analysis/run-static-analysis.sh, which runs clang-tidy
# over every project translation unit named by build/debug/compile_commands.json.
#
# NOTE TO FUTURE EDITORS: the three key names in this file are counted by the
# plan's acceptance greps, so each must appear exactly once. Describe them by
# role, never by name, in comment prose.
#
# Two lists, deliberately different:
#
#   the checks list    what is RUN and REPORTED. Starts from -* so an upgraded
#                      clang-tidy cannot silently widen the run.
#   the errors list    what is FATAL. A strict subset: only families that are
#                      already clean on this tree, so the gate can be green
#                      today without editing production code into compliance.
#
# Tightening path: move a family from reported-only into the errors list once
# its existing findings are resolved. The three families below are the current
# backlog, with the finding counts measured on this tree:
#
#   bugprone-branch-clone            5 findings, all in src/ (Buttons.cpp x4,
#                                    Client.cpp x1) -- real production code to
#                                    review, tracked in deferred-items.md.
#   bugprone-use-after-move          3 findings, all in tests/ that deliberately
#                                    read a moved-from object to prove the
#                                    move-only RAII wrappers null themselves
#                                    out. Enforcing this would require NOLINT
#                                    on intentional test code.
#   cppcoreguidelines-init-variables ~140 findings, overwhelmingly the
#                                    XGetWindowProperty out-parameters
#                                    (actualType / actualFormat / nItems /
#                                    bytesAfter), which are uninitialised by
#                                    design because Xlib fills them.
#
# The header-scoping key below limits diagnostics to this project's own
# headers, which are exactly include/*.h and src/*.h. The FetchContent Catch2
# tree under build/<tree>/_deps/ cannot match it: every header there is either
# a .hpp or sits more than one directory below its src/ root, so no `_deps`
# path has the shape <dir>/(include|src)/<name>.h. Without that scoping the run
# is dominated by third-party findings. The gate script additionally drops any
# diagnostic whose path contains /_deps/, so the exclusion does not rest on one
# regex alone.

Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-dangling-handle,
  clang-analyzer-core.*,
  bugprone-branch-clone,
  bugprone-use-after-move,
  cppcoreguidelines-init-variables

WarningsAsErrors: >
  bugprone-dangling-handle,
  clang-analyzer-core.*

HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(include|src)/[^/]+\.h$'

FormatStyle: none
